{"id":"7501f91fafe45522","group":"58","path":"58/batch17/58-thm-projective-hierarchy.md","title":"Structure of the Lightface Projective Hierarchy","display":"thm-projective-hierarchy — Structure of the Lightface Projective Hierarchy","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-projective-hierarchy","aliases":["58-thm-projective-hierarchy","Lightface Projective Hierarchy"],"display":"thm-projective-hierarchy — Structure of the Lightface Projective Hierarchy","depends_on":["[[58-df-lightface]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-projective-hierarchy"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-projective-hierarchy</span><span>Lightface Projective Hierarchy</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-projective-hierarchy — Structure of the Lightface Projective Hierarchy"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"255364c0a7fc9610\" href=\"?note=255364c0a7fc9610\" title=\"58-df-lightface\">58-df-lightface</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal N=\\omega^\\omega\">\\(\\mathcal N=\\omega^\\omega\\)</span> (Baire space)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma^1_n,\\Pi^1_n,\\Delta^1_n\">\\(\\Sigma^1_n,\\Pi^1_n,\\Delta^1_n\\)</span> (lightface projective pointclasses, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"255364c0a7fc9610\" href=\"?note=255364c0a7fc9610\" title=\"58-df-lightface\">58-df-lightface</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A^{\\complement_{\\mathcal N}}=\\mathcal N\\setminus A\">\\(A^{\\complement_{\\mathcal N}}=\\mathcal N\\setminus A\\)</span> (complement in Baire space)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\pi_{\\mathcal N}(B)=\\{x\\in\\mathcal N:\\exists y\\in\\mathcal N\\;(\\langle x,y\\rangle_{\\mathcal N}\\in B)\\}\">\\(\\pi_{\\mathcal N}(B)=\\{x\\in\\mathcal N:\\exists y\\in\\mathcal N\\;(\\langle x,y\\rangle_{\\mathcal N}\\in B)\\}\\)</span> (effective-pairing projection from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"255364c0a7fc9610\" href=\"?note=255364c0a7fc9610\" title=\"58-df-lightface\">58-df-lightface</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}projective\\text{-}hierarchy}\\vdash\n\\forall n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\n\\left[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\Pi^1_n\n&amp;=\\{A\\subseteq\\mathcal N:A^{\\complement_{\\mathcal N}}\\in\\Sigma^1_n\\},\\\\\n\\Sigma^1_{n+1}\n&amp;=\\{\\pi_{\\mathcal N}(B):B\\in\\Pi^1_n\\},\\\\\n\\Delta^1_n\n&amp;=\\Sigma^1_n\\cap\\Pi^1_n,\\\\\n\\Sigma^1_n\\cup\\Pi^1_n\n&amp;\\subseteq\\Delta^1_{n+1}.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\right]\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}projective\\text{-}hierarchy}\\vdash\n\\forall n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\n\\left[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\Pi^1_n\n&amp;=\\{A\\subseteq\\mathcal N:A^{\\complement_{\\mathcal N}}\\in\\Sigma^1_n\\},\\\\\n\\Sigma^1_{n+1}\n&amp;=\\{\\pi_{\\mathcal N}(B):B\\in\\Pi^1_n\\},\\\\\n\\Delta^1_n\n&amp;=\\Sigma^1_n\\cap\\Pi^1_n,\\\\\n\\Sigma^1_n\\cup\\Pi^1_n\n&amp;\\subseteq\\Delta^1_{n+1}.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\right]\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>This statement is entirely lightface; boldface pointclasses allow real parameters and must not be mixed into the same recursion.</li>\n<li>Complementation exchanges the <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma\">\\(\\Sigma\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Pi\">\\(\\Pi\\)</span> sides, while projection advances from <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Pi^1_n\">\\(\\Pi^1_n\\)</span> to <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma^1_{n+1}\">\\(\\Sigma^1_{n+1}\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>The effective pairing <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal N^2\\cong\\mathcal N\">\\(\\mathcal N^2\\cong\\mathcal N\\)</span> is part of the upstream definition, so every displayed pointclass remains a collection of subsets of the same carrier.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-lightface","status":"resolved","id":"255364c0a7fc9610","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-lightface]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-lightface","status":"resolved","id":"255364c0a7fc9610","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\Sigma^1_n,\\Pi^1_n,\\Delta^1_n$ (lightface projective pointclasses, see [[58-df-lightface]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-lightface","status":"resolved","id":"255364c0a7fc9610","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\pi_{\\mathcal N}(B)=\\{x\\in\\mathcal N:\\exists y\\in\\mathcal N\\;(\\langle x,y\\rangle_{\\mathcal N}\\in B)\\}$ (effective-pairing projection from [[58-df-lightface]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathcal N=\\omega^\\omega","display":false},{"tex":"\\Sigma^1_n,\\Pi^1_n,\\Delta^1_n","display":false},{"tex":"A^{\\complement_{\\mathcal N}}=\\mathcal N\\setminus A","display":false},{"tex":"\\pi_{\\mathcal N}(B)=\\{x\\in\\mathcal N:\\exists y\\in\\mathcal N\\;(\\langle x,y\\rangle_{\\mathcal N}\\in B)\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}projective\\text{-}hierarchy}\\vdash\n\\forall n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\n\\left[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\Pi^1_n\n&=\\{A\\subseteq\\mathcal N:A^{\\complement_{\\mathcal N}}\\in\\Sigma^1_n\\},\\\\\n\\Sigma^1_{n+1}\n&=\\{\\pi_{\\mathcal N}(B):B\\in\\Pi^1_n\\},\\\\\n\\Delta^1_n\n&=\\Sigma^1_n\\cap\\Pi^1_n,\\\\\n\\Sigma^1_n\\cup\\Pi^1_n\n&\\subseteq\\Delta^1_{n+1}.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\right]","display":true},{"tex":"\\Sigma","display":false},{"tex":"\\Pi","display":false},{"tex":"\\Pi^1_n","display":false},{"tex":"\\Sigma^1_{n+1}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal N^2\\cong\\mathcal N","display":false}],"bytes":1624,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4375","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch17/58-thm-projective-hierarchy.md|58-thm-projective-hierarchy]]（batch17）"},{"id":"7334957c6d59eacc","anchor":"ref-241","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[58-thm-0-sharp.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-condensation.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-definability.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-generic-extension.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-is-transitive.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-satisfies-GCH.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-satisfies-ZFC.md]]\n[[58-thm-MM.md]]\n[[58-thm-V-equal-L.md]]\n[[58-thm-V-equals-L.md]]\n[[58-thm-absoluteness-calculation.md]]\n[[58-thm-ac-wellorder-equivalent.md]]\n[[58-thm-aleph-properties.md]]\n[[58-thm-analytic-completeness.md]]\n[[58-thm-analytic-set-properties.md]]\n[[58-thm-baire-category-theory.md]]\n[[58-thm-baire-category.md]]\n[[58-thm-banach-tarski.md]]\n[[58-thm-beth-function-properties.md]]\n[[58-thm-boolean-valued-model.md]]\n[[58-thm-borel-cardinality.md]]\n[[58-thm-borel-determinacy-proof.md]]\n[[58-thm-bounded-forcing-axioms.md]]\n[[58-thm-cantor.md]]\n[[58-thm-cardinal-multiplication.md]]\n[[58-thm-club-filter-properties.md]]\n[[58-thm-club-guessing.md]]\n[[58-thm-club-intersection-proper.md]]\n[[58-thm-club-intersection.md]]\n[[58-thm-coanalytic-separation.md]]\n[[58-thm-coding-universe.md]]\n[[58-thm-cofinality-regular.md]]\n[[58-thm-cohen-forcing-CH.md]]\n[[58-thm-collapse-forcing.md]]\n[[58-thm-compactness.md]]\n[[58-thm-consistency-strength-hierarchy.md]]\n[[58-thm-continuum-hypothesis.md]]\n[[58-thm-countable-choice.md]]\n[[58-thm-covering-lemma.md]]\n[[58-thm-dense-set-lemma.md]]\n[[58-thm-dependent-choice.md]]\n[[58-t